## Why a dedicated importer

`pdc_sales_private.import_sales_accessories_20261020(text,jsonb,jsonb,text)` stays the Broome writer (prosrc md5 `46d4b464c5c1800c8ada245fb2d33bd3`). It hardcodes dealer `37047`, looks up a receipt by file sha alone, and inserts lines onto tables whose dealer check is `37047`. A dealer argument on that body, or sharing those tables, can write Broome Sales. Karratha rows go to `karratha_sales_accessory_receipts`, `karratha_sales_accessory_lines` and `karratha_sales_accessory_vehicle_status`. Each dealer check is `14450` only. The Broome check is not widened. The Karratha import body does not contain `37047`.

`import_karratha_sales_orders` is the Navision orders feed. It does not exist on staging and this release does not create it. Department 135 (`karratha/`, `karratha135_pdc`) is not edited.

## Function

```
pdc_sales_private.import_karratha_sales_accessories_20261025(
  p_action text,
  p_envelope jsonb,
  p_rows jsonb DEFAULT NULL,
  p_expected_preview_hash text DEFAULT NULL
) RETURNS jsonb
```

Identity: `pdc_sales_private.import_karratha_sales_accessories_20261025(text,jsonb,jsonb,text)`.

Prosrc md5 `c70dc4234952dfb58cbc022c98bcecdb`.

Management connection only. No execute grant for `anon`, `authenticated` or `service_role`.

`p_action` is `match`, `manifest`, `preview`, `apply` or `readback`. `match` is the no-write dry run (no receipt row). `manifest` stores the receipt. `preview` stores `preview_hash` only. `apply` needs that hash and writes only the Karratha tables, dealer `14450`. `readback` counts those rows. Re-importing the same file sha with the same payload and snapshot is a no-op. The same Outlook message id with a different sha returns `message_id_sha_conflict` and writes nothing. A newer snapshot replaces lines for a matched stock. An older snapshot does not. Stocks missing from a later file keep their current lines.

Match is the latest applied Microsoft Navision batch for dealer `14450`, current rows, COSI yes, not hidden, and not a deleted vehicle link. One visible order per stock. Unmatched stocks are in the summary and are not inserted. `vehicles_created`, `jobs_created` and `bookings_created` are 0. No insert into `public.vehicles`, jobs, bookings or Navision.

`get_accessories()` returns the Karratha read when the sales context dealer is `14450`, and the existing Broome query when it is `37047`. Any other dealer stays empty. The Karratha read runs before `build_stock_counts()`, which still raises unless the dealer is `37047`. New prosrc md5 `ff5de642f867c80b62d6c3fef987f131` (was `2f7f060cdaca01cc2763a15b921debf8`, r495). The Sales page still calls `get_broome_sales_accessories`. On `?branch=karratha` the roster is the branch roster (CF and SL) and the Broome delay checkbox is not rendered. `setDelay` does not call `set_broome_sales_accessory_delay` from that branch, because that RPC writes dealer `37047`.

## How to call it with the pdc@ envelope

After go-live, on a management connection:

```sql
SELECT pdc_sales_private.import_karratha_sales_accessories_20261025(
  'match',
  jsonb_build_object(
    'source_kind','karratha_sales_deal_items_workbook',
    'sheet','Results',
    'header_row',4,
    'headers','["Quote #","Stock #","PO Line","Price Level Desc","Notes","PO #","Transaction Sub-Type","Transaction Type"]'::jsonb,
    'extract_text','Extracted on Sunday, October 25, 2026 @ 5:27 PM ... Dept = "105" ... Dept = "107"',
    'extract_tz','Australia/Perth',
    'file_sha256','<64 hex chars of the .xls bytes>',
    'file_name','KTA Allocation - Deal Items - Job 1.xls',
    'mailbox','pdc@pmgwa.com.au',
    'sender','noreply@revolutionsoftware.com.au',
    'internet_message_id','<01dd6462$Blat.v3.2.22$f930ee15$18e03ba91696@10.255.11.20>',
    'received_at','2026-10-25T09:27:15Z',
    'source_rows',2458,
    'dealer_code','14450'
  ),
  '<jsonb array of the 2458 row objects>'::jsonb
);
```

`gmail_message_id`, `outlook_message_id` or `microsoft_message_id` is accepted in place of `internet_message_id` (r508: hex of any length, or length 8–512 with no whitespace). `dealer_code` may be omitted or `014450`. A `Dealer` column, Dept 110, Dept 112 or Dept 135 in the extract, or any other mailbox or sender, is refused. Do not call `import_sales_accessories_20261020` for this file.

Then `manifest` with the same envelope and rows, `preview` with the sha (rows may be null), and `apply` with `p_expected_preview_hash` set to the preview hash.

